! FLASH1 as examples/flash1/flash1.bmad states it, with the undulators integrated rather
! than period-averaged, for the frame-series measurement of docs/performance.md. The
! machine is that file's and unchanged. fel_method is Bmad's own element attribute, so
! it is set here and every other Bmad program still loads the lattice.
!
! ds_step is a fifth of an undulator period. It does not set the integration, which is
! run.unaveraged_steps_per_period at twenty substeps a period whatever this says. It sets
! how often the field and the slippage are advanced, and the comb cannot be finer than it.

call, file = ../../examples/flash1/flash1.bmad

wiggler::*[fel_method] = unaveraged
wiggler::*[ds_step] = 0.00546
